## 21. IMPLEMENTATION WORKFLOW

Complete the redesign in the following order.

### Phase 1: Project inspection
Inspect the existing project and identify templates, CSS, JavaScript, views, and URLs that require updates.

### Phase 2: Global design system
Implement colors, typography, spacing, buttons, forms, cards, and shared layout styles.

### Phase 3: Header and navigation
Update the main header, search bar, account menu, cart count, category navigation, and welcome popup.

### Phase 4: Homepage
Implement the hero banner, category shortcuts, promotional sections, product carousels, and footer.

### Phase 5: Product pages
Redesign product listing, filters, product cards, category pages, and product details.

### Phase 6: Cart and checkout
Update cart and checkout layouts without breaking authentication, inventory validation, or Razorpay.

### Phase 7: Customer pages
Update login, registration, profile, order history, and order tracking.

### Phase 8: Admin dashboard
Redesign dashboard cards, tables, charts, navigation, inventory management, customer management, and order management.

### Phase 9: Responsive optimization
Test desktop, tablet, and mobile layouts.

### Phase 10: Functional verification
Test every important button, link, form, filter, modal, cart action, checkout step, and admin action.

Fix visual regressions and functional issues before completion.

